# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Karigar AI — FRONTEND environment (Vite reads these as import.meta.env.*)
#
#   cp frontend/.env.example frontend/.env
#
# EVERYTHING WORKS WITHOUT THESE. If the Firebase vars are blank, the app runs
# auth in a local "demo account" mode — "Skip for now (demo)" and even the
# Google/phone buttons fall back to a local account, so a login/Firebase
# misconfig can NEVER block the stage demo.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Backend base URL (optional) -----------------------------------------
# Usually left blank: the app defaults to http://localhost:8000 (web) or
# http://10.0.2.2:8000 (Android emulator). Set it to bake in a LAN IP.
# VITE_API_BASE=http://192.168.1.42:8000

# --- Firebase Web SDK (optional — enables REAL Google + phone-OTP sign-in) --
# Create a project at https://console.firebase.google.com, enable the
# Google and Phone sign-in providers under Authentication, then copy these
# from Project settings → Your apps → SDK setup and configuration.
#
# IMPORTANT: add your dev/demo origin (e.g. localhost, your LAN IP, and the
# Capacitor WebView origin https://localhost) under Authentication →
# Settings → Authorized domains, or Google popup + phone OTP will be rejected.
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=      # your-project.appspot.com (optional)
